   'Which method is commonly used in forest tree improvement to evaluate the genetic merit of different tree families under controlled environmental conditions?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Mass selection"},{"id":"b","text":"Progeny testing"},{"id":"c","text":"Natural regeneration"},{"id":"d","text":"Gene conservation"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01172', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In a breeding program focused on the improvement of Shorea species, what is a major challenge associated with polyploidy?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Increased susceptibility to pests and diseases"},{"id":"b","text":"Reduced growth rates compared to diploid species"},{"id":"c","text":"Limited availability of genetic material"},{"id":"d","text":"Complexity in genetic analysis and breeding strategies"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01173', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'What is the primary benefit of using molecular markers in forest genetics and tree improvement programs?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"They provide a visual assessment of tree health."},{"id":"b","text":"They allow for the precise identification of genetic variations."},{"id":"c","text":"They enhance the aesthetic value of forest landscapes."},{"id":"d","text":"They increase the volume of wood production per hectare."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01174', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In the genetic improvement of native tree species, what is the significance of maintaining a high level of genetic diversity within breeding populations?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To ensure the rapid growth of all individuals."},{"id":"b","text":"To increase the uniformity of physical traits."},{"id":"c","text":"To decrease the need for artificial selection."},{"id":"d","text":"To enhance resilience to environmental changes and diseases."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01175', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'Which of the following is the primary goal of a clonal test in forest tree improvement?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To evaluate the growth performance of different clones under standardized conditions."},{"id":"b","text":"To increase genetic diversity within a plantation."},{"id":"c","text":"To assess the disease resistance of individual trees."},{"id":"d","text":"To measure the carbon sequestration capacity of clones."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fe-g01176', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In forest tree improvement, what is the significance of assessing the heritability of a trait?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It helps to estimate the cost of breeding programs."},{"id":"b","text":"It provides an overview of environmental factors affecting growth."},{"id":"c","text":"It indicates the nutritional needs of the species."},{"id":"d","text":"It determines the potential success rate of selecting for that trait."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01177', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In the context of forest genetics, what is the main advantage of employing a provenance trial?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To enhance the aesthetic value of forests."},{"id":"b","text":"To conserve all genetic lines equally."},{"id":"c","text":"To identify the best performing genetic sources for specific environments."},{"id":"d","text":"To reduce the breeding cycle of trees."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fe-g01178', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In tree improvement programs, what does the term ''plus tree'' refer to?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"A tree that grows faster than any known species."},{"id":"b","text":"A tree that contributes to soil fertility."},{"id":"c","text":"A tree that attracts more wildlife."},{"id":"d","text":"A tree with superior characteristics selected for propagation."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01179', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In forest genetics, what does the term ''gene flow'' refer to?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"The random change in allele frequencies within a population."},{"id":"b","text":"The loss of genetic diversity due to environmental changes."},{"id":"c","text":"The development of new genetic variations through mutation."},{"id":"d","text":"The process of alleles being transferred from one population to another."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01180', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In forest genetics, what advantage does genetic variation provide to a population of trees?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Enhances resilience to diseases and environmental stresses."},{"id":"b","text":"Increases the likelihood of pest outbreaks."},{"id":"c","text":"Decreases adaptability to environmental changes."},{"id":"d","text":"Reduces the growth rate of the population."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fe-g01181', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In tree improvement programs, what is the role of a clone bank?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To enhance the genetic diversity of a wild population."},{"id":"b","text":"To promote natural regeneration of forest trees."},{"id":"c","text":"To increase the carbon sequestration potential of forests."},{"id":"d","text":"To preserve and store genetic material of superior genotypes."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01182', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'What is a progeny test in the context of tree improvement?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"An evaluation of a tree''s resistance to pests and diseases."},{"id":"b","text":"A test to determine the growth rate of a single tree."},{"id":"c","text":"An assessment of the genetic quality of offspring from selected parents."},{"id":"d","text":"A measurement of the total biomass produced by a tree stand."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fe-g01183', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'Which tree species is commonly used in the Philippines for genetic improvement due to its durability and high-quality timber?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Pinus kesiya (Benguet Pine)"},{"id":"b","text":"Pterocarpus indicus (Narra)"},{"id":"c","text":"Swietenia macrophylla (Mahogany)"},{"id":"d","text":"Gmelina arborea (Gmelina)"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01184', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In forest genetics, which factor is primarily considered when selecting plus trees for a breeding program?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Tree''s geographical location"},{"id":"b","text":"Tree''s root depth"},{"id":"c","text":"Tree''s overall height and diameter growth"},{"id":"d","text":"Tree''s leaf color"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fe-g01185', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'Why is controlled pollination important in tree breeding programs?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To increase genetic variation by allowing random pollination."},{"id":"b","text":"To ensure the propagation of only the most genetically superior trees."},{"id":"c","text":"To reduce the cost of tree breeding programs."},{"id":"d","text":"To decrease the time required for tree maturation."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01186', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'What is the main purpose of using molecular markers in forest genetics?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To visually identify tree species."},{"id":"b","text":"To directly influence the physical growth of trees."},{"id":"c","text":"To map out geographical distribution of trees."},{"id":"d","text":"To assess genetic diversity and relatedness among tree populations."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01187', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'What is a major risk of low genetic diversity in tree populations?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Increased resistance to diseases"},{"id":"b","text":"Greater adaptability to environmental changes"},{"id":"c","text":"Higher susceptibility to pests and diseases"},{"id":"d","text":"Enhanced reproductive success"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fe-g01188', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In forest genetics, what is meant by the term ''phenotypic plasticity''?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"The ability of trees to change their genetic makeup over generations."},{"id":"b","text":"The capacity of a tree genotype to express different phenotypes in response to environmental conditions."},{"id":"c","text":"The ability of a population to remain genetically stable despite environmental changes."},{"id":"d","text":"The tendency of trees to revert to their ancestral form."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01189', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In tree improvement, what is the significance of assessing genetic gain?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To evaluate the physical aesthetics of trees."},{"id":"b","text":"To determine the historical growth rates in native forests."},{"id":"c","text":"To quantify the carbon sequestration capacity of a forest stand."},{"id":"d","text":"To measure the increase in desirable traits achieved through selection and breeding."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01190', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In forest genetics, which term refers to the occurrence of similar traits among related individuals more frequently than expected by chance, due to shared ancestry?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Genetic correlation"},{"id":"b","text":"Genetic linkage"},{"id":"c","text":"Genetic drift"},{"id":"d","text":"Genetic bottleneck"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fe-g01191', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'Which technique in tree improvement involves selecting trees based on observable characteristics to improve forest traits in future generations?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Hybridization"},{"id":"b","text":"Phenotypic selection"},{"id":"c","text":"Mutation breeding"},{"id":"d","text":"Cytoplasmic inheritance"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01192', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In the context of tree improvement, what is a major advantage of using vegetative propagation over seed propagation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Increased genetic diversity"},{"id":"b","text":"Faster multiplication of select genotypes"},{"id":"c","text":"Greater adaptability to new environments"},{"id":"d","text":"Resistance to environmental stress"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01193', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In forest genetics, what does the term ''heterosis'' refer to?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Reduction in fitness due to mating between closely related individuals"},{"id":"b","text":"Adaptation to a specific environmental condition"},{"id":"c","text":"Increased vigor and growth rate in hybrid offspring compared to their parents"},{"id":"d","text":"Formation of new species through hybridization"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fe-g01194', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'What is the primary goal of using a seed orchard in tree improvement programs?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To provide a controlled environment for genetic mutation studies"},{"id":"b","text":"To conserve endangered tree species"},{"id":"c","text":"To facilitate natural cross-pollination among diverse species"},{"id":"d","text":"To maximize the production of superior seeds for reforestation"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01195', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'Which concept in forest genetics involves maintaining a balance between conserving genetic diversity and improving specific desirable traits?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Gene conservation"},{"id":"b","text":"Genetic gain"},{"id":"c","text":"Breeding balance"},{"id":"d","text":"Genetic equilibrium"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fe-g01196', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'What is the main purpose of employing marker-assisted selection in tree breeding programs?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To identify environmental stress factors"},{"id":"b","text":"To reduce the incidence of genetic drift"},{"id":"c","text":"To increase the overall population size of the species"},{"id":"d","text":"To accelerate the selection of desirable traits"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01197', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In the context of forest genetics, what is a potential drawback of relying solely on hybridization techniques for tree improvement?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Reduced genetic variability in the long term"},{"id":"b","text":"Increased susceptibility to pests"},{"id":"c","text":"Slower growth rates than pure species"},{"id":"d","text":"Higher production costs"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fe-g01198', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In tree improvement, which principle involves the use of genetic information to plan the mating of selected trees to enhance specific traits?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Cytogenetics"},{"id":"b","text":"Genomic selection"},{"id":"c","text":"Quantitative trait locus mapping"},{"id":"d","text":"Population genetics"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01199', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In forest genetics and tree improvement, which term best describes the genetic material transferred from one tree to another through pollen?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Gametes"},{"id":"b","text":"Alleles"},{"id":"c","text":"Genes"},{"id":"d","text":"Propagules"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fe-g01200', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In the context of tree improvement, what is the purpose of backcrossing in a breeding program?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To introduce new genetic material from a wild relative into a domesticated population"},{"id":"b","text":"To assess the heritability of traits across generations"},{"id":"c","text":"To reduce inbreeding depression by introducing genes from unrelated populations"},{"id":"d","text":"To increase the frequency of desirable traits in a population by crossing a hybrid with one of its parents"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01201', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In tree improvement programs, which selection method involves evaluating the performance of offspring to determine the genetic value of their parents?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Phenotypic selection"},{"id":"b","text":"Progeny selection"},{"id":"c","text":"Provenance selection"},{"id":"d","text":"Clonal selection"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01202', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In the context of tree breeding, which of the following describes the primary purpose of a genetic gain trial?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To evaluate the adaptability of a species to different climatic conditions."},{"id":"b","text":"To determine the best planting density for maximum yield."},{"id":"c","text":"To assess the genetic diversity within a breeding population."},{"id":"d","text":"To compare the growth performance of improved versus unimproved genotypes."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01203', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'Which of the following processes in forest genetics involves the assessment of genotype by environment interaction to optimize tree selection for specific site conditions?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Genotype-environment trials"},{"id":"b","text":"Provenance trials"},{"id":"c","text":"Backcrossing"},{"id":"d","text":"Clonal propagation"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fe-g01204', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In forest tree improvement, what is the significance of a half-sib family test?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It evaluates the performance of trees with known parentage from a common father but different mothers."},{"id":"b","text":"It measures the genetic diversity among unrelated trees."},{"id":"c","text":"It determines the adaptability of clones to different environments."},{"id":"d","text":"It assesses the disease resistance of a population."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fe-g01205', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'When conducting a recurrent selection program for tree breeding, what is the primary goal of testing the offspring from selected parents?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To assess the genetic gain from one generation to the next."},{"id":"b","text":"To ensure high survival rate under adverse conditions."},{"id":"c","text":"To maintain genetic diversity across generations."},{"id":"d","text":"To identify trees with unique phenotypes for further breeding."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fe-g01206', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In forest genetics, what is the role of a field trial in a tree improvement program?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To evaluate the genetic diversity within a seed stand."},{"id":"b","text":"To test the growth and adaptability of different tree genotypes under natural environmental conditions."},{"id":"c","text":"To compare different soil treatments for tree growth."},{"id":"d","text":"To measure the carbon sequestration potential of a forest stand."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01207', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'Why is it important to include both control and improved varieties in a progeny test within a tree improvement program?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To determine the best time of year for planting."},{"id":"b","text":"To monitor pest and disease resistance."},{"id":"c","text":"To ensure high germination rates."},{"id":"d","text":"To compare the genetic gain achieved through breeding."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01208', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In the genetic improvement of dipterocarps, what is a common challenge associated with using seed-based propagation methods?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"High rate of seed dormancy."},{"id":"b","text":"Difficulty in controlling pollination."},{"id":"c","text":"Low genetic variation among seeds."},{"id":"d","text":"Incompatibility with other species."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01209', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'What is the primary distinction between half-sib and full-sib tests in tree breeding programs?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Half-sib tests are conducted over a shorter duration."},{"id":"b","text":"Half-sib tests focus on pest resistance, while full-sib tests focus on growth rate."},{"id":"c","text":"Full-sib tests require controlled environment conditions."},{"id":"d","text":"Full-sib tests involve offspring from the same mother and father, while half-sib tests involve offspring from the same father but different mothers."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01210', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In tree improvement, which genetic principle involves selecting individuals based on their overall genetic merit to enhance desired traits in future generations?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Index selection"},{"id":"b","text":"Pedigree selection"},{"id":"c","text":"Mass selection"},{"id":"d","text":"Family selection"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fe-g01211', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'Which concept in forest genetics refers to the statistical measure of the proportion of phenotypic variation that is attributable to genetic variation in a population?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Genetic drift"},{"id":"b","text":"Heritability"},{"id":"c","text":"Gene flow"},{"id":"d","text":"Genetic bottleneck"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01212', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In the context of forest genetics, what is the main reason for conducting a genotype by environment interaction study in tree improvement programs?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To determine the best performing clone across all environments."},{"id":"b","text":"To understand how different genotypes respond to varying environmental conditions."},{"id":"c","text":"To identify tree species that can thrive in monoculture plantations."},{"id":"d","text":"To increase the seed production of selected tree species."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01213', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In a tree improvement program, why is it important to assess both additive and non-additive genetic variances?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To ensure that genetic diversity is completely eliminated."},{"id":"b","text":"To ensure that only non-additive traits are selected for improvement."},{"id":"c","text":"To measure the height of trees more accurately."},{"id":"d","text":"To optimize the selection process for traits that can be directly improved by breeding."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01214', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'When implementing a recurrent selection program in the genetic improvement of Tectona grandis (teak), what is a primary objective?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To decrease the overall genetic diversity in the population."},{"id":"b","text":"To produce clones with identical genetic makeup."},{"id":"c","text":"To continually increase the frequency of favorable alleles in the population."},{"id":"d","text":"To enhance the resilience of the species to all types of pests."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fe-g01215', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In the genetic improvement of Acacia mangium, how can molecular markers assist in the early selection of superior genotypes?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By identifying phenotypic traits that are easily observable."},{"id":"b","text":"By facilitating the direct measurement of wood density."},{"id":"c","text":"By eliminating the need for field trials altogether."},{"id":"d","text":"By allowing the association of specific markers with desirable traits."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01216', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'What is the primary purpose of using a multi-site trial in the genetic improvement of dipterocarps in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To discourage the use of hybrid species in forest plantations."},{"id":"b","text":"To select the best performing genotypes across diverse environments."},{"id":"c","text":"To homogenize the genetic makeup of all tree populations."},{"id":"d","text":"To study the impact of climate change on tree growth."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fe-g01217', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'Which of the following best describes the role of heterozygosity in the genetic improvement of forest trees?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It helps in maintaining a high level of genetic variation within a population."},{"id":"b","text":"It reduces the genetic diversity of the population."},{"id":"c","text":"It ensures that all members of the population are genetically identical."},{"id":"d","text":"It eliminates the need for any form of genetic testing."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fe-g01218', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In a breeding program for Gmelina arborea, what is a key advantage of using controlled cross-pollination over open pollination?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It increases the number of seeds produced per tree."},{"id":"b","text":"It reduces the cost of establishing plantations."},{"id":"c","text":"It eliminates the need for any genetic screening."},{"id":"d","text":"It enables precise control over the genetic makeup of the offspring."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fe-g01219', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'What is the benefit of conducting a diallel cross in a tree improvement program?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To identify the best performing individual tree without considering family performance."},{"id":"b","text":"To reduce the genetic diversity within a breeding population."},{"id":"c","text":"To evaluate the general combining ability of multiple parent trees."},{"id":"d","text":"To focus only on phenotypic traits without genetic analysis."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fe-g01220', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In forest genetics, why is it important to maintain a balance between genetic gain and genetic diversity during tree improvement?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To prevent genetic drift from becoming the dominant evolutionary force."},{"id":"b","text":"To ensure rapid adaptation to environmental changes."},{"id":"c","text":"To maximize genetic gain at the expense of diversity."},{"id":"d","text":"To eliminate all inferior genetic variations."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fe-g01221', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'When selecting mother trees for a seed orchard, why is it crucial to assess their progeny performance in multiple environments?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To ensure that the selected mother trees produce seeds that are genetically identical."},{"id":"b","text":"To increase the physical resemblance among all progeny."},{"id":"c","text":"To verify that the progeny exhibit consistent performance across different sites."},{"id":"d","text":"To reduce the cost of seed production in the orchard."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fe-g01222', 'forest-ecosystem', 'forest-genetics-tree-improvement', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In the context of forest genetics and tree improvement, which term describes the process of selecting and breeding trees based on their ability to consistently produce high-quality timber across different environments, and what is the underlying genetic principle that supports this practice?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Provenance Trials; focused solely on identifying the best local genotypes without considering broader adaptability."},{"id":"b","text":"Genotype x Environment Interaction; it highlights the importance of selecting genotypes that perform well across a range of environmental conditions."},{"id":"c","text":"Genetic Drift; a random process that does not contribute to systematic improvement of traits."},{"id":"d","text":"Inbreeding Depression; a genetic principle that is unrelated to environmental adaptability but focuses on the reduction of fitness due to breeding between closely related individuals."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00474', 'forest-governance', 'forest-history', 'Easy', 'mock',
   'In what year was the Forest Management Bureau (FMB) established in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"1987"},{"id":"b","text":"1997"},{"id":"c","text":"1977"},{"id":"d","text":"2007"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00475', 'forest-governance', 'forest-history', 'Easy', 'mock',
   'Which law is known as the Revised Forestry Code of the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Republic Act No. 8371"},{"id":"b","text":"Republic Act No. 7586"},{"id":"c","text":"Presidential Decree No. 1151"},{"id":"d","text":"Presidential Decree No. 705"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00476', 'forest-governance', 'forest-history', 'Easy', 'mock',
   'What is the primary purpose of Republic Act No. 7586 in Philippine forestry?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Establishing seed production areas"},{"id":"b","text":"Creating the National Integrated Protected Areas System (NIPAS)"},{"id":"c","text":"Regulating the use of chainsaws"},{"id":"d","text":"Reforming forest fees and charges"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00477', 'forest-governance', 'forest-history', 'Easy', 'mock',
   'Which act is known as the Indigenous Peoples'' Rights Act in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Republic Act No. 7586"},{"id":"b","text":"Republic Act No. 8371"},{"id":"c","text":"Republic Act No. 9147"},{"id":"d","text":"Republic Act No. 9175"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00478', 'forest-governance', 'forest-history', 'Easy', 'mock',
   'What is the focus of Republic Act No. 9175, enacted in 2002, in the context of forestry?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Wildlife conservation"},{"id":"b","text":"Community-based forest management"},{"id":"c","text":"Chainsaw regulation"},{"id":"d","text":"Reforestation efforts"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00479', 'forest-governance', 'forest-history', 'Easy', 'mock',
   'What is Republic Act No. 9147 known for in Philippine forestry history?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Wildlife Resources Conservation and Protection Act"},{"id":"b","text":"Chainsaw regulation"},{"id":"c","text":"National Greening Program"},{"id":"d","text":"Establishment of the Forest Management Bureau"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00480', 'forest-governance', 'forest-history', 'Easy', 'mock',
